  "takes": [
    {
      "@type": "Take",
      "scene": "Philipp wants to know when a new dotsloth version is out and to update easily. The CLI is installed globally via npm.",
      "decided": [
        {
          "@type": "Decision",
          "text": "Notify after every command (via BaseCommand.finally) when a newer version exists on npm, one dim line: \"dotsloth X.Y.Z available — run: dotsloth update\""
        },
        {
          "@type": "Decision",
          "text": "Suppress notification on the update command itself (this.id !== 'update')"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Decision",
          "text": "Cache the npm registry check in state.json for 24h so it does not add latency on every run; only the first run after 24h does a network call"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Decision",
          "text": "dotsloth update runs npm install -g @phibar/dotsloth@<latest>; on failure prints the manual command"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Decision",
          "text": "State stored in ~/.config/dotsloth/state.json (PATHS.localState, already defined, previously unused)"
        }
      ],
      "wordsGiven": [
        {
          "@type": "Word",
          "text": "src/lib/state.ts, src/lib/update-check.ts, src/core/update.ts, src/commands/update.ts, src/cli/base-command.ts (finally hook added)."
        }
      ],
      "discussed": [
        "Background fetch considered but avoided: fetch keeps the event loop alive; instead the check runs at the end of the command and awaits with a 5s timeout — acceptable since it happens at most once per 24h after the command's own output is done",
        "isNewer uses numeric semver comparison (not string) to handle 1.0.10 > 1.0.9"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
